fs (wasi): fewer host mode calls per created file (homescoop, the KC's install trace)

slicc-kernel's trace of an install showed pnpm's wasm port spending
about a third of its per-file OPFS calls on modes:
- create_inheriting_mode (every store file) looked up its shard
  directory's mode (lmode) each time: now once per directory per run;
- grant_file_mode then fstat'ed the new file (fmode) to see whether the
  umask narrowed its mode, and copy_file_exclusive (every imported file)
  re-applied the mode it created the file with (fchmod).
Both are skipped when the umask clears none of the mode's bits and the
host has been seen to apply creation modes: the first such file is still
checked, so a host that ignores the creation mode keeps the old path.

